commit 0aa17893c2efcd699348a0e72294d4cd5dafcd90
Author:     Eshan Iyer <79593316+eshankiyer@users.noreply.github.com>
AuthorDate: Mon Aug 31 05:37:56 2026 -0400
Commit:     Eshan Iyer <79593316+eshankiyer@users.noreply.github.com>
CommitDate: Mon Aug 31 05:37:56 2026 -0400

    feat(parity): round 14 lane A coverage pass on the fresh 1-2 lead tail
    
    Round 14 exhausted the standard 8-40 lead band across every prior round's
    attempted-method set (verified zero fresh leads remain for the six core
    classes: Entity, LivingEntity, Player, BlockBehaviour, Mob, ItemStack), so
    this round pulls from the previously-untouched 1-2 lead tail: recipe book
    packets, legacy RNG, structure template placement, dried ghast, turtle egg,
    datapack/recipe book loading, long-jump goal, shulker bullet, wind charge,
    brush, spawn egg, and the place-recipe packet handler.
    
    Fixes surfaced during gating:
    - wind_charge.rs: tick_deflect_cooldown used `(ticks > 0).then_some(ticks -
      1)` - then_some's argument is eager, so `ticks - 1` evaluated even when
      ticks was 0, panicking on subtract-overflow. Verified against
      WindCharge.java:44-49 (tick() only decrements while noDeflectTicks > 0);
      the Rust logic's intent was correct, only the eager evaluation was a bug.
      Switched to `ticks.checked_sub(1)`.
    - turtle_egg.rs: test module imported BlockProperties from the crate root;
      the trait lives at pumpkin_data::block_properties::BlockProperties.
    - shulker_bullet.rs: should_despawn compared a Difficulty enum by == inside
      a const fn, which isn't const-stable for a derived PartialEq; switched to
      matches!().
    - brush.rs: on_use_tick's stack parameter was named _stack but genuinely
      read in the method body; removed the underscore.
    - structure_template.rs: set_random marked const fn (clippy).

