commit 3ff591bfa94ca4546f31da7889de3f49b2e72d90
Author:     Eshan Iyer <79593316+eshankiyer@users.noreply.github.com>
AuthorDate: Sun Aug 23 21:04:24 2026 -0400
Commit:     Eshan Iyer <79593316+eshankiyer@users.noreply.github.com>
CommitDate: Sun Aug 23 21:04:24 2026 -0400

    fix(parity): vine bonemeal growth, wither summon, slime step, spawner XP, dispensers
    
    Nether vines (twisting/weeping vines): implement bonemeal (isValidBonemealTarget,
    isBonemealSuccess, performBonemeal - GrowingPlantHeadBlock.java:113-134) with the
    geometric block count from NetherVines.getBlocksToGrowWhenBonemealed
    (NetherVines.java:14-22).
    
    Fixed during review: bonemeal_grow_plant_head never advanced its "current head"
    position across iterations, so growing more than one block left a stack of head
    blocks instead of a single head with body segments filling in behind it.
    
    WitherSkullBlock: switch the summon-base check from hardcoded soul sand/soil to the
    real WITHER_SUMMON_BASE_BLOCKS tag (WitherSkullBlock.java:94-121); add canSpawnMob
    for the dispenser path.
    
    Fixed during review: the base-pattern check never verified the two cells beside the
    bottom base block are air (aisle("   ", "###", "~#~")'s `~` cells), so a solid block
    there wouldn't correctly block a summon; the wither spawned one block too high
    (getBlock(1, 2, 0) is the pattern's bottom row, not the middle "top_middle" row this
    used).
    
    SlimeBlock: port stepOn's horizontal velocity damping (SlimeBlock.java:30-37) and gate
    fallOn's zero-damage callback on not sneaking, matching isSuppressingBounce/
    isSteppingCarefully (both just isShiftKeyDown, Entity.java:2681-2687).
    
    SpawnerBlock: award popExperience's 15+2d15 XP on player-mined break when drops are
    allowed (SpawnerBlock.spawnAfterBreak, SpawnerBlock.java:41-47; Block.popExperience,
    Block.java:445-449).
    
    Fixed during review: the XP orb spawned at the block's raw corner position instead of
    its center (Vec3.atCenterOf(pos)), inconsistent with the other block-XP call sites in
    this codebase.
    
    DispenserBlock: dispense wither skeleton skulls through WitherSkullBlock.canSpawnMob
    (DispenseItemBehavior.java:229-247), matching the carved-pumpkin dispense pattern.
    Documented gap: the dispensed skull doesn't inherit the dispenser's facing as its
    rotation (cosmetic only).

